WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.350
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.106
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.406 --> 00:00:15.600
Unit four: Hobbies & Interests. Today you will talk about hobby goals with want to and would like to.

4
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.471
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:22.771
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:24.432
Passion.

7
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:28.066
Passion means a very strong love for something.

8
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.185
Music is my passion.

9
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:33.308
Your turn. Say: Passion.

10
00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:36.970
Passion.

11
00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:38.428
Talent.

12
00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:42.461
Talent means a natural ability to do something well.

13
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.748
She has a talent for singing.

14
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.782
Your turn. Say: Talent.

15
00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:51.472
Talent.

16
00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:52.962
Craft.

17
00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.251
Craft means making things with your hands.

18
00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.175
Weaving is a traditional Khmer craft.

19
00:00:59.783 --> 00:01:01.902
Your turn. Say: Craft.

20
00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:05.443
Craft.

21
00:01:06.183 --> 00:01:07.266
Photography.

22
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.935
Photography means taking pictures with a camera.

23
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.700
I learn photography on my phone.

24
00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:17.143
Your turn. Say: Photography.

25
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:20.966
Photography.

26
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:22.602
Collection.

27
00:01:23.617 --> 00:01:25.930
Collection means a group of things you keep.

28
00:01:26.517 --> 00:01:28.412
He has a big stamp collection.

29
00:01:29.017 --> 00:01:31.216
Your turn. Say: Collection.

30
00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.137
Collection.

31
00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:36.954
Skillful.

32
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.449
Skillful means very good at doing something.

33
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.003
My uncle is a skillful painter.

34
00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:46.048
Your turn. Say: Skillful.

35
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.110
Skillful.

36
00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:51.863
Dedicated.

37
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.395
Dedicated means working hard because you care.

38
00:01:55.983 --> 00:01:57.820
She is a dedicated dancer.

39
00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:01.290
Your turn. Say: Dedicated.

40
00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:05.123
Dedicated.

41
00:02:05.883 --> 00:02:07.024
Creative outlet.

42
00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:11.897
Creative outlet means an activity to express your ideas and feelings.

43
00:02:12.483 --> 00:02:14.320
Drawing is my creative outlet.

44
00:02:14.917 --> 00:02:17.766
Your turn. Say: Creative outlet.

45
00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.356
Creative outlet.

46
00:02:23.117 --> 00:02:24.129
Master.

47
00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:27.882
Master means to learn to do something very well.

48
00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:30.344
I want to master the guitar.

49
00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.161
Your turn. Say: Master.

50
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:36.931
Master.

51
00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:38.545
Beginner.

52
00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:42.618
Beginner means a person who is just starting to learn.

53
00:02:43.217 --> 00:02:44.938
I'm a beginner at chess.

54
00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.877
Your turn. Say: Beginner.

55
00:02:50.733 --> 00:02:51.514
Beginner.

56
00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.239
Improve.

57
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.041
Improve means to get better.

58
00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.522
My photos improve every week.

59
00:02:59.117 --> 00:03:01.328
Your turn. Say: Improve.

60
00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:05.400
Improve.

61
00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.151
Showcase.

62
00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:11.369
Showcase means to show something to people in a proud way.

63
00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:14.192
We showcase our art at the school fair.

64
00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:17.157
Your turn. Say: Showcase.

65
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:20.943
Showcase.

66
00:03:21.733 --> 00:03:25.326
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:26.183 --> 00:03:28.229
Visal, what is your passion?

68
00:03:29.317 --> 00:03:32.085
Photography! It's my creative outlet.

69
00:03:33.183 --> 00:03:34.579
Are you skillful at it?

70
00:03:35.683 --> 00:03:39.297
I'm still a beginner, but I'm improving every week.

71
00:03:40.383 --> 00:03:42.302
What would you like to do in the future?

72
00:03:43.417 --> 00:03:48.876
I want to master photography, and I would like to showcase my photos at an exhibition.

73
00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:51.754
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:52.617 --> 00:03:55.266
Grammar focus: want to and would like to.

75
00:03:55.566 --> 00:03:56.765
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.380
I want to master photography.

77
00:04:00.283 --> 00:04:02.190
I would like to showcase my work.

78
00:04:03.083 --> 00:04:04.827
Would you like to join our club?

79
00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:10.323
'Would like to' is more polite than 'want to'. Use it when you ask or offer.

80
00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:14.583
Be careful! Don't say: I would like showcase my work.

81
00:04:16.533 --> 00:04:19.020
Say: I would like to showcase my work.

82
00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.796
Use 'to' after 'would like' before a verb.

83
00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:25.264
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:27.103
My Passion.

85
00:04:27.403 --> 00:04:30.482
Photography is my true passion and creative outlet.

86
00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:34.267
I started as a beginner with my mother's old phone.

87
00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:38.334
I am dedicated, so my photos improve every month.

88
00:04:39.333 --> 00:04:41.101
I want to master light and colour.

89
00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.445
One day, I would like to showcase my talent at an exhibition in Phnom Penh.

90
00:04:47.533 --> 00:04:51.419
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:52.283 --> 00:04:53.923
I would like blank my work.

92
00:04:54.223 --> 00:04:59.386
A, to showcase. B, showcase. C, showcasing.

93
00:05:02.933 --> 00:05:05.003
The answer is A: to showcase.

94
00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:09.241
A natural ability to do something well is a blank.

95
00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:12.904
A, talent. B, craft. C, beginner.

96
00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.246
The answer is A: talent.

97
00:05:19.383 --> 00:05:21.998
To learn to do something very well is to blank.

98
00:05:22.298 --> 00:05:25.894
A, master. B, collect. C, improve.

99
00:05:29.433 --> 00:05:31.201
The answer is A: master.

100
00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.656
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:36.517 --> 00:05:38.969
What hobby would you like to master one day?

102
00:05:47.783 --> 00:05:49.353
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:49.653 --> 00:05:56.183
I would like to master the guitar. I want to play at my school's concert, so I practise every evening.

104
00:05:56.483 --> 00:05:58.286
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:05:59.183 --> 00:06:03.577
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and want to and would like to.

106
00:06:03.877 --> 00:06:08.793
Today's value is dedication. Practise a little every day, and you will get better.

107
00:06:09.093 --> 00:06:11.386
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

108
00:06:11.686 --> 00:06:14.176
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

